femotion does not bundle third-party solvers. Optional extras install them from
their own distributions, under their own licenses:
  - gmsh (extra "mesh"): GNU GPL v2 or later, with exceptions
  - fTetWild through pytetwild (extra "tetwild"): MPL-2.0; pulls in PyVista and
    VTK (MIT, BSD-3)
  - scikit-fem, pyamg (extra "continuum"): BSD-3-Clause, MIT
  - OpenSeesPy (extra "opensees"): OpenSees license, free for educational,
    research and non-profit use; commercial use requires a license from the
    Regents of the University of California
  - MLX (extra "cfd"): MIT, Apple silicon only
  - meshio (extra "io"): MIT
  - sectionproperties (extra "sections"): MIT; its mesher, Shewchuk's Triangle
    (through cytriangle, LGPL-3.0), is free for non-commercial use only and needs
    a license from its author for commercial use
